---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Contact from "../components/Contact.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";

const updated = "29 September 2026";
---

<Base
    title="Privacy & Cookie Policy"
    description={`How ${site.legalName} processes personal data and uses cookies on ${site.url.replace("https://", "")}.`}
>
    <Header base="/" />
    <main id="main">
        <article id="top" class="section legal">
            <div class="legal__inner">
                <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
                <h1 class="display">Privacy &amp; Cookie Policy</h1>
                <p class="legal__meta label">Last updated {updated}</p>

                <h2>1. Data controller</h2>
                <p>
                    {site.legalName}, {site.address.full}. Email: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
                </p>

                <h2>2. What we collect</h2>
                <p>
                    This website has no forms or user accounts. We process personal data only when you
                    contact us by email (your address and the content of your message), to reply to you. The
                    legal basis is our legitimate interest in responding to your request (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR).
                </p>
                <p>
                    If you give consent, we also collect aggregated, pseudonymous usage data through the
                    analytics tools described below (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR).
                </p>

                <h2 id="cookies">3. Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
                <p>
                    <strong>Strictly necessary.</strong> We store your cookie choice in your browser’s local
                    storage (<code>altairith-consent-v1</code>) for up to 6 months. This does not require consent.
                </p>
                <p>
                    <strong>Analytics (only with your consent).</strong> Nothing below is loaded until you
                    choose “Accept all” or enable Analytics in the preferences.
                </p>
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Microsoft Clarity</strong> (Microsoft Corporation) records how visitors use the
                        page, such as clicks, scrolling, and heatmaps. Cookies: <code>_clck</code> (1 year),
                        <code>_clsk</code> (1 day). See the <a
                            href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement"
                            rel="noopener"
                            target="_blank">Microsoft privacy statement</a
                        >.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Google Analytics 4</strong> (Google Ireland Ltd.), when enabled, provides
                        aggregated traffic statistics in Consent Mode v2. It sets <code>_ga</code> and
                        <code>_ga_*</code> cookies (up to 2 years) only after consent. See the <a
                            href="https://policies.google.com/privacy"
                            rel="noopener"
                            target="_blank">Google privacy policy</a
                        >.
                    </li>
                </ul>
                <p>
                    Data processed by these providers may be transferred outside the EEA under the EU–US Data
                    Privacy Framework or Standard Contractual Clauses. Declining analytics does not affect
                    how the site works.
                </p>
                <p>
                    You can change or withdraw your consent at any time via
                    <button type="button" class="legal__link" data-cookie-settings>Cookie settings</button>
                    (also available in the footer of every page).
                </p>

                <h2>4. Retention</h2>
                <p>
                    We keep email correspondence for as long as needed to handle your request and meet legal
                    obligations. Analytics data is kept according to each provider’s retention settings, which
                    is at most 14 months.
                </p>

                <h2>5. Your rights</h2>
                <p>
                    You have the right to access, rectify, erase, restrict, or port your data, to object to
                    processing, and to withdraw consent at any time (Arts. 15–22 GDPR). Write to
                    <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. You can also lodge a complaint with the
                    Italian supervisory authority, the <a
                        href="https://www.garanteprivacy.it"
                        rel="noopener"
                        target="_blank">Garante per la protezione dei dati personali</a
                    >.
                </p>
            </div>
        </article>
        <Contact footerOnly />
    </main>
</Base>

<style>
    .legal {
        padding-top: clamp(140px, 16vw, 200px);
    }
    .legal__inner {
        max-width: 760px;
        margin: 0 auto;
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        gap: 20px;
        color: var(--mist);
    }
    .legal .display {
        color: var(--paper);
        margin-top: 8px;
    }
    .legal__meta {
        color: var(--muted);
        margin-bottom: 24px;
    }
    h2 {
        margin-top: 28px;
        font-family: var(--font-body);
        font-weight: 500;
        font-size: var(--fs-label);
        letter-spacing: var(--ls-wide);
        text-transform: uppercase;
        color: var(--gold);
    }
    strong {
        font-weight: 500;
        color: var(--paper);
    }
    ul {
        margin: 0;
        padding-left: 20px;
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        gap: 12px;
    }
    code {
        font: inherit;
        color: var(--paper);
    }
    a,
    .legal__link {
        color: var(--paper);
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--gold);
    }
    .legal__link {
        background: none;
        border-width: 0 0 1px;
        padding: 0;
        font: inherit;
        cursor: pointer;
    }
    .legal__link:hover {
        color: var(--gold);
    }
</style>
